parents could soon have a new tool to  keep their kids safe pfizer has asked  for fda permission to make its covet  vaccine available for kids as young as  six months old now if authorized  children could start getting the first  of two doses by early march these doses  contain just one tenth the amount that  adults get there is a chance that some  kids will need a third dose after fives  are discovered the two dose regimen may  not be enough in two to four year olds  despite the science many parents still  have a lot of reservations about this  shot nikki bates spoke with two young  kids who have participated in a vaccine  trial  siblings lillian and will love playing  superheroes but last year the two got a  real chance to help others by taking  part in a pfizer covet vaccine clinical  trial helping people is a good thing and  helping people is a good thing  they both got two doses of the vaccine  at cincinnati children's hospital i told  my friends that i was gonna give a shot  lillian was four and will was just three  when they were enrolled they were both  great they both did awesome  their mom sarah says she was grateful  both kids got the vaccine we are so  lucky like who in the world can say that  they were all protected  all ahead of schedule soon millions more  children as young as six months old may  be eligible the fda could make its  decision about authorization in the next  few weeks  but experts don't expect authorization  for kids under five to significantly  affect new case numbers which remain  high that's because only 38 percent of  children who are already eligible are  fully vaccinated once it's clear that  the vaccine is safe and effective people  should feel comfortable using it dr paul  offit a member of the fda's vaccine  advisory committee reassures parents the  process will be thorough we will  carefully look at those data and we will  approve that vaccine for children less  than five only if there is a clear and  robust data set for safety and efficacy  for cbs mornings i'm nikki batiste
 

